    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "Welcome to Burst, the ASCAP podcast. I'm Eric Filberg. Coming up on the podcast today, Oscar, Grammy, and Golden Globe winning Hall of Fame songwriter and ASCAP President Paul Williams talks to the honorable Congressman Adam Schiff of California. They discuss what Congress is doing to include music professionals in coronavirus relief efforts, the need for federal guidelines on restarting live performances at venues, what's at stake in the U.S. Department of Justice's upcoming review of the ASCAP and BMI consent decrees, and how you can join ASCAP in creating positive change for the American music community. That conversation, which took place in July, was part of the ASCAP Experience Home Edition, our summer series of virtual programming designed to inspire, educate, and connect music creators of all stages of their careers. If you miss any of this great series, I've got great news for you. You can watch all of this summer's programming on demand at askapexperience.com forward slash watch now. It's all there, it's all great stuff, check it out. Now check this out. One of the highlights of home edition was this conversation between ASCAP President Paul Williams and Congressman Adam Schiff. Paul, by the way, was our very first guest on the podcast last year. He's also one of the strongest advocates for music creator rights the world has ever seen and has probably logged more miles traveling to DC and walking the halls to talk to legislators on behalf of songwriters than anyone. He's tireless, like the energizer bunny. Here he talks to another great champion for music creators, Adam Schiff. Congressman Schiff represents California's 28th congressional district, and throughout his tenure in Congress, he is focused on growing the economy, bolstering national security, strengthening communities, helping small businesses, improving education, safety, and healthcare for children, and of course helping pass legislation that supports music creators. Currently in his 10th term in the House of Representatives, Schiff is Chairman of the House Intelligence Committee, no small task. With all that going on in our country, Schiff has been hard at work, so we were very fortunate to get some virtual FaceTime with him, so let's jump right in. Here's Paul Williams and Adam Schiff.",
