    "turn_text": "two people may get the same amount of unemployment compensation and the third person may get left out completely. That's really a revelation, I think, to many members of Congress. We wouldn't know about it if people weren't advocating for themselves and organizations like ASCAP weren't bringing it to our attention. So very important, but also You know, as you can imagine, there's great competition for help right now. So many millions of Americans are unemployed. So many millions more have small businesses that are at risk of going under. And if people don't advocate for their members and for themselves, they're much less likely to get the help that they really need. So it's enormously important to reach out to your representatives. to also use the force multiplier that ASCAP is to help educate Congress and advocate for help.",
