    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "We're not all stopping for that little place in Malibu. The fact is that it's a blue collar business for so many. What we do is, I've always said, we're working all because right now we're at a point where to physically stay alive, we social distance, we keep that distance between us, but to stay mentally healthy, to stay emotionally connected, we need a connection that I think music provides in a fashion that is just for you know for no matter how much I clamped down a feeling if you if you show a call a running through the grass and the music is is just right behind it. It will unleash emotions for me the people that I've been studying for years and the like I think that our music is absolutely needed. I think one of the things we're going to need to get the music back up and running is I think that that We're going to need clear national guidelines from the national health, public health officials on exactly how to do this. I think that it's an area that really needs to be addressed. How do we gather? How do we gather safely? I know there's some basics on that that are out there right now that are keeping us alive. But I think to figure out how to move a large amount of people into a venue is something we're going to need help with.",
