    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "You know, I agree. Some things are going to simply take time. The parts of the country where the virus is so widespread, we're going to really have to take quite drastic steps to attain this virus and protect the public. Other places are doing better. Sadly, not too many of them, but there are some states that are doing better where the conditions may be right to reopen venues that you can't reopen elsewhere. But when we do reopen, we need to make sure that we still maintain good standards that we follow best practices. And we're going to need guidance, guidance from experts like the CDC. And, you know, it's, I think, so debilitating when the administration tries to silence the voices of the CDC when they, when they, the president wants to give these briefings now again because he doesn't like his poll numbers. Well, fine. He, you know, a lot of what he says just ain't true. Sometimes it's down way destructive. And, you know, Anthony Fauci may be, you know, down the street and Dr. Birx may be in the next room, but if you don't get to hear from them and what you do get to hear is inaccurate, it doesn't help. In fact, it's permanently hurtful. The CDC, you know, does some great work in establishing these guidelines, but some of those guidelines have been suppressed by this administration.",
