    "turn_text": "people we saw, you know, this goes back to the last pandemic, but it's a good object lesson for us. Those parts of the country in the last pandemic that retained their protections the longest. the social distancing, the wearing of masks that took their time to reopen when they were ready. They recovered faster than those places that race to reopen because in those places that race to reopen, they had a resurgence of the virus. And sadly, that's exactly what we've seen. Those parts of the country that race to reopen when they didn't have the testing and they didn't have the tracing and they weren't ready. And then you add to it all the conflicting messages about wearing masks or not wearing masks. And it was a recipe for the disaster that we're currently experiencing. It didn't have to be this way. We went into this pandemic, the nation on earth best prepared for a pandemic by any objective measure. But sadly, we've had, I think, the worst results.",
