    "episode_id": 49330,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49330.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "You know, one of the side effects of this pandemic and the quarantine is something I want to talk to you about. You know, we learned this some of our nation has so much work to do to advance racial equality. I think that that one of the, I'm reluctant to say gifts of the quarantine, but of the pandemic. But perhaps a gift of the quarantine is that we were a captive audience. And as a captive audience all at home, you know, we saw something on television with a neon on the neck of a gentleman that we could not turn away. And it exploded into what I believe is hopefully a tipping point. and a real change where we can really change as a country and really grow up. I thought when Obama was arrested, was arrested, was elected president. There was that moment when it was like my country is now grown up. I think we should have immense challenges right now. The House passed, and excuse me, if I glance at notes now and then, while I'm the voice of these questions at the moment, there are some spectacular minds that I'm honored to work with who have major input to these questions and they're all important subjects. Rather than looking good, I'd rather do a good job, which is, you know, that's what 30 years sobriety does. I try to do that now. The House passed the Justice and Policing Act and is waiting on the Senate to take it up. Is there more legislative activity we can expect from the House on these issues? Are there other ways our representatives in Congress are joining us in this moment to ensure things finally start to change? I am so proud of ASCAP. Mr. Chairman, I am so proud of ASCAP because we have stepped up to the plate to be totally supportive, you know, of the Black community. And we're collectively to learn to grow, to promote diversity. And I'd love to hear your thoughts on where we go next and how we stay really effective and improve, improve, improve.",
