    "turn_text": "If you are a music creator and are struggling right now, we encourage you to visit ascap.com forward slash music unites us, where you will find coronavirus resources that we hope will help you stay healthy, creative, connected, and financially stable until we can all have in-person jam sessions again. And if you like what you heard today and want to check out more great ASCAP Experience Home Edition sessions, we have them all on demand at askapexperience.com forward slash watch now. You'll find a phenomenal display of the ASCAP community in action because each week brought a fascinating series of conversations directly into people's homes. We heard from Shaggy, T.I., Phineas and Glenn Hansard, Pasek and Paul, Whitney Phillips and Gian Stone, the writers behind the Ariana Grande and Justin Bieber hit Stuck With You, Erika Campbell of Mary Mary, Composers, Hans Zimmer, Michael Abels, Siddhartha Kosla and Amanda Jones, Pulitzer Prize winning songwriter composer Michael R. Jackson, Latin hitmaker Claudia Brandt, Top 40 hitmaker Amy Allen, Country Rock Duo, the Brothers Osborne, love those guys. A conversation between songwriters Dan Wilson and Brandy Clark, a ton of great sound advice sessions to help with your music career, panels on publishing, panels on wellness and so much more. And finally, Summer is here and the time is right for catching some of this season's vibes. Hot Sun, Cold Drinks, great music. ASCAP is pleased to present SPF, an online summer performance festival featuring video performances from an exciting group of some of ASCAP's top songwriters and artists, from buzzworthy up-and-comers to some of our favorite hitmakers from across the musical spectrum. We just released our first show featuring Alyssa Bonogura, Liv and Sebastian Yatra, which you can find at ascap.com forward slash SPF. We'll release new shows on Thursdays, August 13th and 20th. So follow us on social media, grab your flip flops and press play. Thanks to everyone who helped out with this podcast. ASCAP President Paul Williams and Congressman Adam Schiff for the interview, the midnight hours Adrian Young and Ali Shahid Muhammad for her theme music, Aeton Rosenblum for editorial discipline, Rachel Choi for exciting graphic design, Kate Cordova for creative social media support, and Benjamin Keynes of site-sense productions for audio and video editing. If you'd like to check out our show notes, visit ascap.com slash burst. And finally, thanks for listening. Keep the faith and we'll see you back here real soon.",
